{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:\"10.1097/yic.0b013e32832e9b08\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"19584739","source":"MED","pmid":"19584739","doi":"10.1097/yic.0b013e32832e9b08","title":"The effect of prolonged-release melatonin on sleep measures and psychomotor performance in elderly patients with insomnia.","authorString":"Luthringer R, Muzet M, Zisapel N, Staner L.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Luthringer R","lastName":"Luthringer","firstName":"Remy","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"FORENAP Pharma, Rouffach, France."}]}},{"fullName":"Muzet M","lastName":"Muzet","firstName":"Muriel","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Zisapel N","lastName":"Zisapel","firstName":"Nava","initials":"N"},{"fullName":"Staner L","lastName":"Staner","firstName":"Luc","initials":"L"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"5","volume":"24","journalIssueId":1642608,"dateOfPublication":"2009 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2009,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Int Clin Psychopharmacol","title":"International clinical psychopharmacology","essn":"1473-5857","issn":"0268-1315","nlmid":"8609061","isoabbreviation":"Int Clin Psychopharmacol"},"printPublicationDate":"2009-09-01"},"pubYear":"2009","pageInfo":"239-249","abstractText":"Objectives of this study were to investigate the effects of prolonged-release melatonin 2 mg (PRM) on sleep and subsequent daytime psychomotor performance in patients aged > or =55 years with primary insomnia, as defined by fourth revision of the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders of the American Psychiatric Association. Patients (N = 40) were treated nightly single-blind with placebo (2 weeks), randomized double-blind to PRM or placebo (3 weeks) followed by withdrawal period (3 weeks). Sleep was assessed by polysomnography, all-night sleep electroencephalography spectral analysis and questionnaires. Psychomotor performance was assessed by the Leeds Psychomotor Test battery. By the end of the double-blind treatment, the PRM group had significantly shorter sleep onset latency (9 min; P = 0.02) compared with the placebo group and scored significantly better in the Critical Flicker Fusion Test (P = 0.008) without negatively affecting sleep structure and architecture. Half of the patients reported substantial improvement in sleep quality at home with PRM compared with 15% with placebo (P = 0.018). No rebound effects were observed during withdrawal. In conclusion, nightly treatment with PRM effectively induced sleep and improved perceived quality of sleep in patients with primary insomnia aged > or =55 years. Daytime psychomotor performance was not impaired and was consistently better with PRM compared with placebo. PRM was well tolerated with no evidence of rebound effects.","affiliation":"FORENAP Pharma, Rouffach, France.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Sleep Initiation and Maintenance Disorders","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PP","qualifierName":"physiopathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Melatonin","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AD","qualifierName":"administration & dosage"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"TU","qualifierName":"therapeutic use"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Delayed-Action Preparations"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Electroencephalography"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Polysomnography"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Double-Blind Method"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Psychomotor Performance","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Sleep","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Aged"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Aged, 80 and over"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Middle Aged"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Female"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Male"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Surveys and Questionnaires"}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Delayed-Action Preparations","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Melatonin","registryNumber":"JL5DK93RCL"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"abs","site":"www.intclinpsychopharm.com","url":"http://content.wkhealth.com/linkback/openurl?issn=0268-1315&volume=24&issue=5&spage=239"},{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/YIC.0b013e32832e9b08"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":77,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2009-10-09","dateOfCreation":"2009-07-09","dateOfRevision":"2015-11-19","firstPublicationDate":"2009-09-01","firstIndexDate":"2009-10-10","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}